- **src/services/contentstack.ts** (`options`): This is the Stack configuration site — the single contentstack.Stack(options) call at line 91 that every data fetch flows through (via ContentstackFactory). The options object (lines 71-89) currently contains api_key, delivery_token, environment, branch, fetchOptions but NO live_preview block. Adding live_preview here is what enables the SDK to detect preview mode and return draft entries — without it, no downstream consumer can ever receive preview data.  <== **THIS CHANGE PRODUCES THE VALUE** — it is what makes the new or corrected data exist. Without it, every other change here only moves a value that never changed. [runs: both]
  - **Minimal fix:** Add a live_preview block to the options object (lines 71-89): live_preview: { enable: true, preview_token: process.env.CONTENTSTACK_PREVIEW_TOKEN || '' }. Also add CONTENTSTACK_PREVIEW_TOKEN to the env destructuring block (lines 23-36). The existing Stack = contentstack.Stack(options) at line 91 and ContentstackFactory class (line 109) are reused as-is.
- **src/pages/_app.tsx** (`ContentstackContext.Provider`): This is the app-wide provider site where ContentstackContext.Provider wraps the application and sets the context value from server-side page props (header, footer, onboarding, page). For live preview, @contentstack/live-preview-utils must be initialized here with an onEntryChange callback that receives updated entry data from the CMS and pushes it into React state, causing the provider value and all 147+ useContent consumers to re-render. This callback is the PRODUCER of live preview entry data on the client.  <== **THIS CHANGE PRODUCES THE VALUE** — it is what makes the new or corrected data exist. Without it, every other change here only moves a value that never changed. [runs: browser]
  - **Minimal fix:** Import and initialize ContentstackLivePreview from @contentstack/live-preview-utils with { stackSdk: Stack (from src/services/contentstack.ts line 91), onEntryChange: callback }. In the onEntryChange callback, re-fetch the changed entry using the same Stack ContentType/Entry pattern used by ContentstackFactory.createContentTypeEntryQuery (line 185) and update React state (useState) that feeds the ContentstackContext.Provider value. The existing getSingleEntry / getSinglePageEntry pattern from pageService.ts (line 75-88) should be reused for the client-side re-fetch shape.
- **src/context/contentstackContext.tsx** (`ContentstackContext`): The React context that distributes Contentstack data to all components via the useContent hook. Currently createContext<IContentstackContext>({}) with a static interface — the Provider value is set once from server-side props and never updated. For live preview, this context must CARRY reactive state so that when onEntryChange in _app.tsx fires with updated entry data, all useContent consumers re-render with new values.  (carries the value — moves or re-exposes what something else produced) [runs: browser]
  - **Minimal fix:** Add a setContent or updatePage callback field to IContentstackContext (line 8-18) so the onEntryChange subscriber in _app.tsx can push updated entry data into the context. The existing context shape (header, footer, onboarding, page, pagesBaseURLs, directories, languageAlternativePageSlug) is reused — only an updater mechanism is added.
- **src/components/pages/Homepage.tsx** (`Homepage`)  [NO EDIT REQUIRED — part of the fix, correctly left unchanged]: Target page per acceptance criteria (MX Homepage). Receives page prop (IContentstackPage[]) and renders ContentStackHomePageHeroBanner, HomepageComponentMapper, ContentstackRecentNews, ContentStackLandAcknowledgement. Child components use useContent hook which reads from ContentstackContext. Once the context becomes reactive via onEntryChange, Homepage and all its children will automatically re-render with preview data — no direct edit needed.  (verify only — no edit expected here) [runs: browser]
  - **Minimal fix:** No code change required. Homepage reads page data from props at line 21 and its children consume useContent from ContentstackContext. When the context value updates (from onEntryChange subscription in _app.tsx), Homepage re-renders automatically. Verify that the page prop and context page data stay synchronized when live preview updates arrive — the context page field (IContentstackContext.page at line 12) must reflect the updated entry.
- **src/services/pageService.ts** (`PageService.getPageEntry`)  [NO EDIT REQUIRED — part of the fix, correctly left unchanged]: Server-side data fetcher (lines 166-229) that populates the page prop passed to ContentstackContext.Provider. Calls getSinglePageEntry (line 211) or getSingletonPageEntry (line 212) which delegate to getSingleEntry/getSingletonEntry from contentstack.ts. This is the existing server-side pipeline that live preview augments client-side. The getSinglePageEntry function (line 75-88) uses getSingleEntry with contentstackConfig lookup — this same pattern should be reused in the onEntryChange callback for client-side re-fetching of preview entries.  (verify only — no edit expected here) [runs: server]
  - **Minimal fix:** No code change needed for server-side fetching. The onEntryChange callback in _app.tsx should reuse the same getSingleEntry pattern (via ContentstackFactory.createContentTypeEntryQuery from src/services/contentstack.ts line 185) for client-side re-fetches. Verify that contentstackConfig (referenced at line 80) and ContentTypes constants are accessible client-side for the callback to resolve contentTypeUid config.
- **src/hooks/useContent.ts** (`useContent`)  [NO EDIT REQUIRED — part of the fix, correctly left unchanged]: The hook used by 147+ components to read Contentstack data via ContentstackContext. Returns getContentByKey which path-navigates the context value using getValue. Once the context value becomes reactive (updated by onEntryChange in _app.tsx), all useContent consumers will automatically re-render — no change needed here. This is the verification point to confirm the full pipeline works end-to-end.  (verify only — no edit expected here) [runs: browser]
