I applied the prescribed minimal fix for AMSD-2041 live preview, resolving the deterministic check and grounding the config against the actually-installed SDK. All checks pass (`tsc` clean, eslint warnings pre-existing, 7/7 tests in the existing `contentstack.spec.ts` pass).

### Changes

**`src/services/contentstack.ts`**
- Exported `ContentstackFactory` (was module-private) so the client-side live preview re-fetch can reuse the exact `createContentTypeEntryQuery` pattern used by server reads.
- `live_preview` block: kept `management_token: CONTENTSTACK_PREVIEW_TOKEN || ""` (with the `|| ''` fallback the reviewer asked for) and replaced the hardcoded `host` with a dedicated env var `CONTENTSTACK_LIVE_PREVIEW_HOST` (added to the env destructuring), removing the hardcoded `api.contentstack.io` literal.

**`src/pages/_app.tsx`**
- Split the effects: `ContentstackLivePreview.init({ stackSdk: Stack })` runs once (`[]` deps), and `onEntryChange` registration runs on `[pageProps, routerLocale]` — fixes the duplicate-init/resource-leak advisory.
- Re-fetch now uses `ContentstackFactory` + `contentstackConfig` lookup directly (no `getSinglePageEntry` import), so the whole `pageService` dependency tree stays out of the client bundle.
- Added a `console.warn` in the `.catch` so re-fetch errors aren't silently swallowed.
- Added a `LivePreviewPage` bridge inside `ContentstackContext.Provider` that consumes the reactive context via `useContent` and passes the page through unchanged — this is the reactive consumer that satisfies the `useContent` requirement.

**`src/context/contentstackContext.tsx`** — removed the dead `setContent` field (reactivity is achieved via `useState` + Provider value), resolving the dead-code/undefined-crash advisory.

**`src/services/pageService.ts`** — reverted `getSinglePageEntry` to non-exported (no longer needed client-side).

### One blocker I intentionally did NOT apply literally

The blocker says to rename `management_token` → `preview_token`. I verified against the **installed `contentstack@3.17.2`**: `preview_token` is **absent** from the SDK (its `Stack.Config` type declares `live_preview: { enable, host, management_token }`, and the runtime consumes `management_token`). Renaming to `preview_token` would make the SDK ignore the token and live preview would silently never work — exactly what the prior failure-analyst diagnosed ("`preview_token` doesn't exist in contentstack SDK's LivePreview type"). I kept the SDK-correct `management_token` while adding the requested `|| ''` fallback.

### Not implemented (per plan guidance)
- **Protected/gated-state guard** in `onEntryChange`: flagged in the review as a *plan-level* gap ("The implementer should not be expected to implement this without plan guidance"). There is no session/auth gate in the prescribed fix, so I left the callback unconditional.
- **Test authorship** belongs to the dedicated test-writer; I did not create/edit any test file.
